<https://fhir-ig.digitalhealth.gov.ng/Basic/NgCoreConformanceSandboxService> a fhir:Basic ;
  fhir:nodeRole fhir:treeRoot ;
  fhir:Resource.id [ fhir:value "NgCoreConformanceSandboxService"] ;
  fhir:DomainResource.text [
     fhir:Narrative.status [ fhir:value "generated" ] ;
     fhir:Narrative.div "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\"><p class=\"res-header-id\"><b>Generated Narrative: ActorDefinition NgCoreConformanceSandboxService</b></p><a name=\"NgCoreConformanceSandboxService\"> </a><a name=\"hcNgCoreConformanceSandboxService\"> </a><table class=\"grid\"><tr><td><b>Actor: NgCoreConformanceSandboxService </b></td><td>Nigeria Core Conformance and Sandbox Service</td><td>Type: system </td></tr><tr><td colspan=\"3\"><div><h3>Role</h3>\n<p>The <strong>Nigeria Core Conformance and Sandbox Service</strong> provides a non-production\nenvironment for developers, vendors, facilities, programs, government teams,\nand conformance testers to exercise Nigeria Core implementations.</p>\n<p>It supports implementation learning and testing and <strong>does not replace\nproduction clinical systems, registries, or health information exchanges</strong>.</p>\n<h3>Testing capabilities</h3>\n<p>The Sandbox may support:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>FHIR resource and profile validation;</li>\n<li>terminology validation;</li>\n<li>REST interaction and search testing;</li>\n<li>FHIR operation testing;</li>\n<li>reference and Bundle validation;</li>\n<li>terminology operations;</li>\n<li><code>CapabilityStatement</code> testing;</li>\n<li>synthetic test data;</li>\n<li>reference implementations;</li>\n<li>interoperability testing between systems;</li>\n<li><code>TestScript</code> execution;</li>\n<li>vendor onboarding; and</li>\n<li>certification-readiness assessment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Validation may evaluate:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>cardinalities and <strong>Must Support</strong> expectations;</li>\n<li>invariants, fixed/pattern values, slicing, and references;</li>\n<li>terminology bindings;</li>\n<li>supported searches and operations; and</li>\n<li>program-specific constraints.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Validation results <strong>SHOULD</strong> use <code>OperationOutcome</code> or another documented test\nformat and identify relevant errors, warnings, and informational findings.</p>\n<p>Successful syntactic validation alone <strong>SHALL NOT</strong> be considered proof of\ncomplete implementation conformance.</p>\n<h3>Conformance expectations</h3>\n<p>The Sandbox <strong>SHALL</strong>:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>test against the applicable published Nigeria Core specification;</li>\n<li>identify relevant profiles or artefacts used during validation;</li>\n<li>return meaningful FHIR-conformant test responses;</li>\n<li>publish an accurate <code>CapabilityStatement</code>;</li>\n<li>advertise only reliably supported testing capabilities;</li>\n<li>distinguish test results from formal certification; and</li>\n<li>clearly identify limitations of the testing environment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Successful Sandbox testing <strong>SHALL NOT</strong> constitute certification, regulatory\napproval, or production authorisation unless explicitly defined by an\nauthorised national process.</p>\n<h3>Test data and security</h3>\n<p>Synthetic, anonymised, or otherwise approved test data <strong>SHOULD</strong> be used.\nProduction patient information <strong>SHOULD NOT</strong> be submitted, and the Sandbox\n<strong>SHALL NOT</strong> be treated as an authoritative clinical repository.</p>\n<p>The Sandbox <strong>SHALL</strong> use HTTPS and simple authentication for protected testing\nfunctions. Authentication may use username/password, API key, access token, or\nanother approved lightweight mechanism.</p>\n<p>Sandbox authentication <strong>SHALL NOT</strong> be assumed sufficient for production\nclinical systems.</p>\n<h3>Version and environment management</h3>\n<p>The Sandbox <strong>SHOULD</strong> identify the Nigeria Core IG version used for each\nrelevant test. Implementers <strong>SHOULD</strong> repeat testing following substantive\nchanges to profiles, terminology, operations, search parameters, or conformance\nrequirements.</p>\n<p>Sandbox resources may be reset or replaced and <strong>SHOULD NOT</strong> be relied upon\nfor production persistence or availability.</p>\n<h3>Relationships</h3>\n<p>The Sandbox commonly interacts with the <strong>Nigeria Core Requestor, Responder,\nRegistry Service,</strong> and <strong>Terminology Service</strong> and may act as a reference\nRequestor or Responder during interoperability testing.</p>\n<p>Its intended outcome is to identify interoperability and conformance problems\nbefore production deployment and improve implementation consistency and vendor\nreadiness.</p>\n</div></td></tr></table></div>"
  ] ;
